Reuse-distance hooks for PHP 5.0.0's Zend allocator (docs/plans/2026-11-15-php-reuse-distance.md).
The hooked file includes php-reuse-gap.h, which defines the five hook macros as nothing unless
EXP_REUSE_GAP is defined. The hooks record the block header, the address Zend itself works with,
at _emalloc's two hand-outs (AG(cache) and malloc), _efree, _efree's free to malloc, a
successful _erealloc and request shutdown's frees. Every change rewrites an existing line (the
include takes a blank one) away from the nested layer's seven substitutions, so no line moves
and that patch still applies to the hooked file at fuzz 0 and without offset (build.sh checks it).

